.policy "ruff-ret506-superfluous-else-raise" revision 2
.description "Remove the else or elif after an if branch that raises, and dedent its code; the branch already leaves the function."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff RET506 (flake8-return): an `elif` or `else` right after an `if` body whose first jump is a `raise`. That
// branch leaves the function, so the rest can be dedented. Only an if's first elif/else clause is
// paired with its body, and only the body's own statements are looked at, in order: the first return, raise,
// break or continue decides which rule fires. Checked in each def RET reads (python/flow-return); reported
// at the keyword.
//   if x:
//       raise ValueError
//   else:                      ← RET506 "Unnecessary `else` after `raise` statement"
//       y()
#include "python/flow-return.rr"

.violation RET506(at: span, w: symbol) code "RET506" "Unnecessary `{w}` after `raise` statement"
    suppress ruff "RET506"
RET506(kw, w) :- else_after_jump(kw, w, "raise").
